Scenario: bin/fm-secondmate-restart.sh default FM_SECONDMATE_PERSIST_WAIT is
90s, not 900s (fix commit 199aa99), against a deaf secondmate (never answers
the persist doorbell).

Driven live with the real bin/fm-secondmate-restart.sh, the real
fm-pending-reply-lib.sh gate, and the fm-secondmate-restart.test.sh session
stub, WITHOUT overriding FM_SECONDMATE_PERSIST_WAIT (so the script's own
default applies) against one never-answering local mate.

$ bash /tmp/scenario-restart-default-timeout.sh
RESULT rc=3 elapsed=92s
nudged: sm1: it did not confirm within 90s that its open work is written down, so its conversation was not spent
summary: 0 of 1 restarted, 1 nudged, 0 unreached
PASS: default persist wait honored ~90s (was 900s before fix)

Conclusion: a deaf secondmate now falls back to the honest nudge path after
~90s wall-clock, matching the new default in bin/fm-secondmate-restart.sh
(PERSIST_WAIT=${FM_SECONDMATE_PERSIST_WAIT:-90}). Before the fix the default
was 900s, matching the captain's reported 600s/900s EXIT=124 hangs on `mmp`.
